  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - Golomoti Solar Power Project, through Power Engineers, Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A USTDA grant to Golomoti JCM Solar Corporation partially funds a feasibility study (Study) to assess the viability of a 17.5 to 40 MW solar power project in the Golomoti district of Malawi (Project). The Study will determine the size of the solar facility and whether an energy storage system is appropriate for co-location on the Project site. The implementation of the project will result in an increase in and diversification of electricity generation in Malawi, a country with one of the world&apos;s lowest electrification rates. Power Engineers, Incorporated, a U.S. engineering firm, is performing the Study.</narrative>
  </description>
